From: nuwa bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] 8796-nuwa-cs-observe (opt-in, off by default)

Adds nuwa_cs_config(), a read-only accessor for the file-static cs_config record, so the
SystemOS diagnostics can report the code-signing configuration dyld/AMFI run under.
Compiled only with -DXNU_NUWA_CS_OBSERVE=1; without it no symbol or string exists.
Apply with -p1 in the XNU tree root.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_codesigning.c	2026-11-18 00:50:20.364642191 +0800
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_codesigning.c	2026-11-18 00:50:20.364728543 +0800
@@ -56,6 +56,20 @@
 SYSCTL_UINT(_security_codesigning, OID_AUTO, monitor, CTLFLAG_RD, &cs_monitor, 0, "code signing monitor type");
 SYSCTL_UINT(_security_codesigning, OID_AUTO, config, CTLFLAG_RD, &cs_config, 0, "code signing configuration");
 
+#if defined(XNU_NUWA_CS_OBSERVE) && XNU_NUWA_CS_OBSERVE
+/*
+ * nuwa r20: read-only accessor for the code-signing configuration record.  cs_config is
+ * file-static, so a diagnostic in another translation unit cannot read it otherwise; this
+ * returns exactly the value the security.codesigning.config sysctl reports and changes no
+ * state.  Compiled only with -DXNU_NUWA_CS_OBSERVE=1.
+ */
+uint32_t
+nuwa_cs_config(void)
+{
+	return os_atomic_load(&cs_config, relaxed);
+}
+#endif
+
 void
 code_signing_configuration(
 	code_signing_monitor_type_t *monitor_type_out,
